WEBVTT

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:46.200
It's been a month since
I started at Ayanagi Academy.

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:51.540
I've got regular classes, Team Otori
practices, and independent training.

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:55.370
It's a lot of work every day,
but I'm also having a lot of fun.

00:00:55.370 --> 00:00:59.830
Little by little, I'm starting to make friends
with the other members of the team, too.

00:00:59.830 --> 00:01:01.080
Go, me!

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:06.120
After this pain, the fat will
magically turn into muscle...!

00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:11.950
Tsukigami?

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:19.250
Morning, Tsukigami!

00:01:23.080 --> 00:01:25.910
Morning! Surprised to see me?

00:01:28.580 --> 00:01:31.750
Don't interrupt. You'll throw off my rhythm.

00:01:32.540 --> 00:01:34.000
Sorry...

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:39.250
Stupid Hoshitani!

00:01:39.250 --> 00:01:42.500
Jeez, why didn't you wake me up?!

00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:44.000
♪Kaito Tsukigami♪
♪Shu Kuga♪

00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:49.160
Your phone kept ringing.

00:01:49.160 --> 00:01:50.660
Thanks.

00:01:56.370 --> 00:01:57.040
♪Mother♪
♪Cell♪

00:01:57.040 --> 00:01:59.000
She's so persistent.

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:05.120
Hello?

00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:09.750
I've told you a million times. There's no reason
for me to go to Haruto's award ceremony...

00:02:11.790 --> 00:02:14.540
Fine, fine.

00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:17.370
Okay. Bye.

00:02:20.790 --> 00:02:22.540
♪Theater Journal♪ ♪Special Report: Haruto Tsukigami♪
♪Youngest Winner of Theater's Top Award♪

00:02:32.330 --> 00:02:35.910
<i>D-R-E-A-M-E-R, Dreamer</i>

00:02:35.910 --> 00:02:43.250
<i>Clicking my heels on the pavement after the rain</i>

00:02:43.250 --> 00:02:50.370
<i>With light steps,</i>
<i>in high spirits, my heart leaps</i>

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:58.250
<i>♪Purely, delightfully, humorously♪</i>

00:02:58.250 --> 00:02:59.750
<i>Wow oh Wow oh</i>

00:02:59.750 --> 00:03:06.290
<i>That's my motto</i>

00:03:06.290 --> 00:03:14.540
<i>If I'm going to move forward without</i>
<i>doing anything and break into pieces</i>

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:20.790
<i>Then I'll go for broke, I won't look back</i>

00:03:20.790 --> 00:03:21.830
<i>Go! Go!</i>

00:03:21.830 --> 00:03:29.290
<i>If I just keep looking at it,</i>
<i>my dream will remain a dream</i>

00:03:29.290 --> 00:03:33.000
<i>I don't want to give up,</i>
<i>don't want to have regrets</i>

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:38.790
<i>I don't know how, but it's not impossible</i>

00:03:38.790 --> 00:03:43.200
<i>I'm a Dreamer.</i>

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:44.450
♪STARMYU♪
<i>I'm a Dreamer.</i>

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:48.000
♪STARMYU♪
<i>D-R-E-A-M-E-R, Dreamer</i>

00:03:51.790 --> 00:03:55.500
<i>D-R-E-A-M-E-R, Dreamer</i>

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:57.790
♪Act 4♪

00:03:57.790 --> 00:03:59.750
I'm starving!

00:03:59.750 --> 00:04:01.830
What's today's Nayuki Lunch?

00:04:01.830 --> 00:04:05.370
I overslept this morning,
so it's just rice balls. Sorry.

00:04:05.370 --> 00:04:07.370
Rice balls are the best!

00:04:08.910 --> 00:04:10.620
I wonder who that is?

00:04:22.700 --> 00:04:24.700
Wow...

00:04:24.700 --> 00:04:26.870
Wow, you're amazing!

00:04:26.870 --> 00:04:28.870
Kuga, you can play the piano?

00:04:28.870 --> 00:04:31.910
Just through self-study. I'm not that good.

00:04:31.910 --> 00:04:34.160
You can play that well without any lessons?

00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:36.660
I thought it was someone
from the piano department.

00:04:36.660 --> 00:04:41.200
I know! Let's practice our dance
moves with Kuga's accompaniment.

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:42.830
I refuse.

00:04:52.790 --> 00:04:54.700
The noodles will get soggy.

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:59.950
Kuga, is that all you're eating for lunch?

00:04:59.950 --> 00:05:00.750
Something wrong with that?

00:05:00.750 --> 00:05:05.620
No, but is that enough?

00:05:05.620 --> 00:05:07.950
My body gets good mileage.

00:05:07.950 --> 00:05:11.700
Kuga, please have some if you'd like!

00:05:24.410 --> 00:05:26.290
Thanks, I appreciate it.

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:30.330
Sure!

00:05:30.330 --> 00:05:31.410
Thanks for the food!

00:05:31.410 --> 00:05:32.700
Thanks.

00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:35.910
This morning's Tsukigami was seriously amazing!

00:05:35.910 --> 00:05:38.370
That's why I have to work hard, too!

00:05:53.410 --> 00:05:55.790
Wow, Hoshitani! Looks good!

00:05:55.790 --> 00:05:56.910
Really?

00:05:56.910 --> 00:05:59.330
You've gotten better.

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:04.910
Isn't that great, Hoshitani?

00:06:04.910 --> 00:06:07.370
It means your practice is paying off!

00:06:07.370 --> 00:06:09.660
It was good of you to practice with him.

00:06:09.660 --> 00:06:13.830
Watching Hoshitani makes me
feel like I need to work hard, too.

00:06:13.830 --> 00:06:17.040
I know! Why don't you join us, too, Kuga?

00:06:39.660 --> 00:06:47.580
♪ I've chosen a narrow path
with just a handful of possibilities ♪

00:06:47.580 --> 00:06:50.000
♪ The warmth enters me ♪

00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:53.700
♪ I am not interested in anything
other than the goal I've decided on ♪

00:06:53.700 --> 00:07:00.620
♪ But the feelings reach even my heart ♪

00:07:00.620 --> 00:07:03.160
♪ On my mind, this encounter ♪

00:07:03.160 --> 00:07:05.750
♪ Goodwill, it won't betray me ♪

00:07:05.750 --> 00:07:10.910
♪ Winding road, on this
path we walk on together ♪

00:07:10.910 --> 00:07:13.370
♪ Border break, they're all different ♪

00:07:13.370 --> 00:07:16.160
♪ Over again, when I get over these walls ♪

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:22.910
♪ Exit, I grab the only
light that makes me shine ♪

00:07:22.910 --> 00:07:26.000
♪ Into the sky that continues to tomorrow ♪

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:28.540
♪ This slight fever is released ♪

00:07:28.540 --> 00:07:33.120
♪ Making our hearts beat together as one ♪

00:07:33.120 --> 00:07:35.040
♪ On the map of dreams ♪

00:07:35.040 --> 00:07:36.200
♪ On your mark! ♪

00:07:36.200 --> 00:07:38.750
♪ Because I have friends ♪

00:07:38.750 --> 00:07:43.660
♪ I will do things my way ♪

00:07:43.660 --> 00:07:52.080
♪ Taking new steps from now on ♪

00:07:55.500 --> 00:07:57.830
I will if I have time.

00:07:57.830 --> 00:08:00.000
All right!

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:03.370
Next is the information session
for the debut performance, right?

00:08:07.370 --> 00:08:10.700
Half of the teams will be cut after this, huh?

00:08:10.700 --> 00:08:14.410
Yes, because the debut
performance is a test stage.

00:08:14.410 --> 00:08:16.040
Let's do our best!

00:08:16.950 --> 00:08:18.080
♪It'll definitely be Team Hiragi.♪

00:08:16.950 --> 00:08:18.080
♪What about the newly formed Star Team?♪

00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:18.700
♪Rumors are that they'd actually failed!♪

00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:19.580
♪Team Otori doesn't stand a chance.♪

00:08:19.580 --> 00:08:20.700
♪I don't think I'd lose to that motley bunch.♪

00:08:20.950 --> 00:08:23.830
Damn it, they're underestimating us!

00:08:27.950 --> 00:08:30.580
Hey, Team Hiragi is here!

00:08:37.700 --> 00:08:39.200
Team Hiragi...

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:41.830
They have a different aura!

00:08:51.450 --> 00:08:53.750
Nayuki, do you know them?

00:08:53.750 --> 00:08:59.370
Tatsumi, Sawatari, Tsukigami,
and I all went to the same junior high.

00:08:59.370 --> 00:09:02.950
Oh, really?

00:09:02.950 --> 00:09:07.080
Why is Tsukigami, who started the year
at the top of the class, on that team?

00:09:07.080 --> 00:09:08.870
I cannot understand.

00:09:08.870 --> 00:09:12.500
I feel bad for him, having
to babysit a team of failures.

00:09:12.500 --> 00:09:15.160
Stop it, Ugawa. They can hear you.

00:09:15.160 --> 00:09:18.750
But it's true, isn't it?
Hey, are you listening, Inumine?

00:09:18.750 --> 00:09:21.450
Huh? What? I wasn't listening.

00:09:22.370 --> 00:09:25.200
They were chosen to be in that group.

00:09:25.200 --> 00:09:27.330
It doesn't matter what you say.

00:09:32.790 --> 00:09:35.000
Bonjour, everyone.

00:09:35.000 --> 00:09:38.870
We will now begin the information session
for the Newcomers' Debut Performance.

00:09:40.620 --> 00:09:44.290
This is the performance of
the first Kao Council members.

00:09:44.290 --> 00:09:47.870
During the debut performance,
not only your singing and dancing,

00:09:47.870 --> 00:09:52.540
but also the organization of your performance
and how well the five of you work together

00:09:52.540 --> 00:09:54.870
will be important factors
in determining your score.

00:09:54.870 --> 00:09:59.750
Because when ensembles come together
in a beautiful way, that is a musical.

00:09:59.750 --> 00:10:01.370
Amazing...

00:10:01.370 --> 00:10:03.160
They're very good.

00:10:03.160 --> 00:10:05.450
Can we do that, too...?

00:10:05.450 --> 00:10:07.450
Hah, it'll be a cinch.

00:10:07.450 --> 00:10:09.120
They've got great expressions on their faces.

00:10:09.120 --> 00:10:11.160
It makes it fun for those watching, too!

00:10:33.000 --> 00:10:34.370
That part's like this, remember?

00:10:34.370 --> 00:10:37.160
Oh, yeah. Thanks!

00:10:37.160 --> 00:10:40.830
Doing a lesson with
everyone's kind of exciting, isn't it?

00:10:40.830 --> 00:10:43.620
Where's Tsukigami?

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:47.200
He left early today.

00:10:47.200 --> 00:10:48.950
Some family business, apparently.

00:10:48.950 --> 00:10:50.790
Family business?

00:10:50.790 --> 00:10:54.620
Oh, his older brother's theater award?

00:10:54.620 --> 00:10:57.500
Older brother? Theater award?

00:10:57.500 --> 00:11:01.120
Haruto Tsukigami graduated
Ayanagi at the top of his class,

00:11:01.120 --> 00:11:05.080
and he's the number one young
musical star out there right now.

00:11:05.080 --> 00:11:08.200
Tsukigami has such an amazing big brother?

00:11:08.200 --> 00:11:11.660
It's not just his brother who's amazing.

00:11:11.660 --> 00:11:14.200
♪23rd Theater Awards - Award Ceremony♪

00:11:11.950 --> 00:11:14.200
The best actor award goes to...

00:11:14.200 --> 00:11:16.370
Haruto Tsukigami!

00:11:21.160 --> 00:11:23.580
His father is a famous theater director,

00:11:23.580 --> 00:11:26.790
and his mother is a stage
actress who represents Japan.

00:11:29.700 --> 00:11:31.370
You came?

00:11:31.370 --> 00:11:34.080
Congratulations on your award, Haruto.

00:11:34.080 --> 00:11:35.660
Thanks.

00:11:35.660 --> 00:11:37.950
How are things with you?

00:11:37.950 --> 00:11:40.700
You made it onto a Star Team, right?

00:11:40.700 --> 00:11:42.660
Yeah, more or less.

00:11:42.660 --> 00:11:45.000
High school will be over before you know it.

00:11:45.000 --> 00:11:47.750
In the end, those who had fun are the winners.

00:11:47.750 --> 00:11:52.000
Well, you've worked harder than
anyone else, so I'm sure you'll be fine.

00:11:52.000 --> 00:11:56.160
It sounds sarcastic coming from a genius.

00:11:56.160 --> 00:11:59.290
Anyway, treasure your friendships.

00:12:43.080 --> 00:12:50.370
♪ I stretched out my hands
to the cloudless sky as a child ♪

00:12:50.370 --> 00:12:57.660
♪ Before I knew it, I had given it up
as a distance I could not reach ♪

00:12:57.660 --> 00:13:04.910
♪ I was always chasing after someone's back ♪

00:13:04.910 --> 00:13:11.450
♪ And the things I had started to look fake ♪

00:13:11.450 --> 00:13:18.790
♪ There was a place I couldn't
reach no matter how much I walked ♪

00:13:18.790 --> 00:13:26.080
♪  rejected the picture of myself that I imagined ♪

00:13:26.080 --> 00:13:33.370
♪ Screaming and crying, praying with all my heart ♪

00:13:33.370 --> 00:13:46.250
♪ Releasing my hoarse voice into the infinite sky ♪
♪ in the limited sky... ♪

00:13:46.250 --> 00:13:49.910
♪ in the limited sky... ♪

00:13:49.910 --> 00:13:56.080
♪ in the limited sky...
in the limited sky... ♪

00:14:04.120 --> 00:14:06.910
♪Kuga | Tsukigami♪

00:14:12.790 --> 00:14:17.120
Hoshitani, I'm going to
buy ingredients for lunch.

00:14:26.450 --> 00:14:28.830
Your big brother's amazing!

00:14:28.830 --> 00:14:32.660
You're so lucky that there's
someone close you can aim for!

00:14:32.660 --> 00:14:35.120
I'll work hard, too, so that one day I'll be--

00:14:35.120 --> 00:14:39.870
♪Work hard, work hard.♪ You sound
like that's all you know how to do!

00:14:51.370 --> 00:14:54.790
I didn't think I'd see a fight scene here.

00:14:54.790 --> 00:15:00.700
I know how irritating it can be to be compared
to and be judged based on those near you.

00:15:00.700 --> 00:15:06.160
But don't take it out on Hoshitani, you boor.

00:15:06.160 --> 00:15:09.290
You're great friends now, huh?

00:15:09.290 --> 00:15:14.290
You know that he's practicing on his
own every day to catch up to us, right?

00:15:14.290 --> 00:15:17.120
So what?

00:15:17.120 --> 00:15:19.750
Hoshitani's not giving up.

00:15:23.040 --> 00:15:27.040
I decided to make enough for everyone
on our team, too, starting tomorrow.

00:15:27.040 --> 00:15:32.000
Hoshitani, do you like
your fried eggs sweet or salty?

00:15:32.000 --> 00:15:34.580
Yeah...

00:15:34.580 --> 00:15:36.250
What's wrong?

00:15:37.750 --> 00:15:41.580
I think I said something
that made Tsukigami mad.

00:15:41.580 --> 00:15:43.870
All I did was talk to him about his brother...

00:15:43.870 --> 00:15:46.370
Oh, that's definitely a taboo subject.

00:15:46.370 --> 00:15:48.410
Huh? Taboo?

00:15:48.410 --> 00:15:52.950
It's legendary how much
Tsukigami hates his brother.

00:15:52.950 --> 00:15:56.160
During the interview the other day,
he rushed out in the middle

00:15:56.160 --> 00:15:59.410
because he was asked about his brother.

00:15:59.410 --> 00:16:01.660
It has nothing to do with it!

00:16:05.000 --> 00:16:07.660
Was that what it was?

00:16:07.660 --> 00:16:09.500
But why?

00:16:09.500 --> 00:16:13.410
If I had a big brother like that,
I'd be so happy and proud.

00:16:13.410 --> 00:16:15.660
It's not about how <i>you</i> feel.

00:16:15.660 --> 00:16:19.410
Shouldn't you think about the
other person's circumstances, too?

00:16:19.410 --> 00:16:21.410
Kuga, welcome back.

00:16:21.410 --> 00:16:25.660
I think everyone has a thing or
two they don't want to talk about.

00:16:36.250 --> 00:16:38.540
High school will be over before you know it.

00:16:38.540 --> 00:16:41.040
In the end, those who had fun are the winners.

00:16:55.160 --> 00:16:57.870
I hope they're happy about the lunches.

00:16:57.870 --> 00:17:01.750
Even if we're teammates,
who would do all that, normally?

00:17:01.750 --> 00:17:04.870
What, you don't want it, Tengenji? Then, I'll--

00:17:04.870 --> 00:17:06.540
I didn't say that!

00:17:13.120 --> 00:17:15.120
Tsukigami?!

00:17:15.120 --> 00:17:17.080
That guy's from Team Hiragi--

00:17:17.080 --> 00:17:18.290
Try saying that again!

00:17:18.290 --> 00:17:20.290
Come on, stop it.

00:17:20.290 --> 00:17:21.950
Shut up!

00:17:23.450 --> 00:17:28.910
I said, you fit right in
with the team of failures.

00:17:28.910 --> 00:17:32.290
I mean, you're just a freebie
that came with your brother.

00:17:32.290 --> 00:17:34.750
Eigo, this has to be stopped.

00:17:34.750 --> 00:17:36.410
But it can't be helped.

00:17:36.410 --> 00:17:39.620
Is that one of the hardships of
having a genius for an older brother?

00:17:39.620 --> 00:17:42.250
Anyone would become twisted.

00:17:53.160 --> 00:17:54.450
That was close!

00:17:54.450 --> 00:17:56.290
Were you trying to punch me just now?

00:17:56.290 --> 00:17:58.910
Just what I'd expect from one of the failures.

00:18:02.410 --> 00:18:06.790
Don't insult my friend.

00:18:06.790 --> 00:18:09.580
I can't help but be treated like a failure.

00:18:09.580 --> 00:18:11.660
But Tsukigami's different.

00:18:11.660 --> 00:18:14.580
As his teammates, we know.

00:18:14.580 --> 00:18:18.250
You don't know anything.
You have no right to talk.

00:18:18.250 --> 00:18:23.370
Friends? What, are you guys playing
at being nice to each other on your team?

00:18:23.370 --> 00:18:23.950
That's just--

00:18:23.950 --> 00:18:25.870
That's enough, Ugawa.

00:18:25.870 --> 00:18:27.700
I apologize, Tsukigami.

00:18:27.700 --> 00:18:29.370
That's just how Ugawa is...

00:18:29.370 --> 00:18:31.950
You think that's good enough?

00:18:31.950 --> 00:18:35.370
After he made a fool of my teammate?!

00:18:38.410 --> 00:18:42.410
You look like you're having fun.
Let me join you.

00:18:43.080 --> 00:18:46.580
Toraishi, I'll be your opponent.

00:18:46.580 --> 00:18:48.910
It's been a while, Shu.

00:18:51.870 --> 00:18:53.580
What should we do, Hoshitani?

00:18:53.580 --> 00:18:54.750
Me, too!

00:18:54.750 --> 00:18:56.790
What?

00:18:56.790 --> 00:18:58.540
Jeez...

00:19:00.370 --> 00:19:02.200
Tsukigami, here.

00:19:02.200 --> 00:19:04.950
Take care of it.

00:19:04.950 --> 00:19:10.910
Oh, that's lunch for everyone that
Nayuki made, so make sure you hang onto it.

00:19:22.870 --> 00:19:24.120
Wait, what?

00:19:24.120 --> 00:19:25.580
What do you mean, ♪what♪?

00:19:25.580 --> 00:19:27.500
You're the cause of this!

00:19:27.500 --> 00:19:29.330
Let go of me!

00:19:49.870 --> 00:19:51.750
What is all this?

00:19:55.330 --> 00:19:57.160
Um, this is...

00:19:57.160 --> 00:20:00.040
...a fight over the lunch Nayuki made!

00:20:00.040 --> 00:20:02.200
Like that'd ever happen!

00:20:09.080 --> 00:20:16.330
Well, you will be informed
of your punishment later.

00:20:16.330 --> 00:20:18.160
I wonder what our punishment will be?

00:20:18.160 --> 00:20:20.000
They were the ones who started it.

00:20:20.000 --> 00:20:21.160
Don't worry about it.

00:20:21.160 --> 00:20:26.370
Man, it must be hard to be
with these savages, Tsukigami.

00:20:26.370 --> 00:20:28.620
You still have to fix your
hang-up about your brother, too.

00:20:28.620 --> 00:20:30.750
Shut up already.

00:20:30.750 --> 00:20:32.660
Let's go.

00:20:34.040 --> 00:20:35.120
Tatsumin!

00:20:35.120 --> 00:20:37.000
Fine...

00:20:45.120 --> 00:20:47.160
Sorry about today.

00:20:47.160 --> 00:20:50.290
Ugawa's not a bad guy, but...

00:20:50.290 --> 00:20:55.250
Tsukigami, if you're worried about
something, you can always come talk to me.

00:20:55.250 --> 00:20:59.660
Aiming for the top by yourself
must be hard, even for you.

00:20:59.660 --> 00:21:02.410
No.

00:21:02.410 --> 00:21:07.450
It doesn't matter if my teammates are
a motley bunch or a bunch of failures.

00:21:07.450 --> 00:21:10.700
I will get past the test
stage with these members.

00:21:10.700 --> 00:21:12.330
That's what I've decided.

00:21:12.330 --> 00:21:14.200
Tsukigami!

00:21:16.620 --> 00:21:19.160
I'll have no mercy on those holding us back!

00:21:19.160 --> 00:21:21.370
All right! Just leave it to me!

00:21:21.370 --> 00:21:25.000
He's saying that because we
<i>can't</i> leave it to you. You boor!

00:21:25.000 --> 00:21:26.370
Huh?

00:21:26.370 --> 00:21:28.660
Don't sound so surprised!

00:21:40.160 --> 00:21:47.370
<i>Someday, when you're crushed by your dreams</i>

00:21:47.370 --> 00:21:53.870
<i>On a night when you look up at a starless sky</i>

00:21:53.870 --> 00:21:57.370
<i>Just remember (today)</i>

00:21:57.370 --> 00:22:01.660
<i>The days we ran like crazy (together)</i>

00:22:01.660 --> 00:22:05.790
<i>Those steps were miracles</i>

00:22:05.790 --> 00:22:09.040
<i>Ring out, Countdown!</i>

00:22:09.040 --> 00:22:12.620
<i>Taking off for the future from here</i>

00:22:12.620 --> 00:22:16.580
<i>You will start singing again</i>

00:22:16.580 --> 00:22:19.750
<i>There are things you lack</i>

00:22:19.750 --> 00:22:23.620
<i>So you reach out desperately to grab them</i>

00:22:23.620 --> 00:22:27.160
<i>These hot, passionate feelings overflowing</i>

00:22:27.160 --> 00:22:30.910
<i>Make the light of the stars your ally</i>

00:22:30.910 --> 00:22:34.450
<i>Even bluffing can become your pride</i>

00:22:34.450 --> 00:22:38.120
<i>You can fly however you want</i>

00:22:38.120 --> 00:22:44.120
<i>Everything starts now!</i>

00:22:59.080 --> 00:23:00.620
Things are going well.

00:23:00.620 --> 00:23:04.330
You're a member of the Kao Council now, huh?

00:23:04.330 --> 00:23:06.910
Tsukigami, sir!

00:23:06.910 --> 00:23:08.790
What are you doing here?

00:23:08.790 --> 00:23:11.330
I'm filming a shoot introducing the school.

00:23:11.330 --> 00:23:13.500
I just went to talk to the chairman.

00:23:13.500 --> 00:23:15.580
Must be hard being a star.

00:23:15.580 --> 00:23:20.080
What about you? If you had taken
the same path as Hiragi and the others,

00:23:20.080 --> 00:23:23.500
you could have been the
leader of the Kao Council.

00:23:25.040 --> 00:23:29.000
I'm not cut out to be a leader.
I'm a problem child even now.

00:23:29.000 --> 00:23:32.370
I've never thought that way about you.

00:23:36.000 --> 00:23:39.450
I'm looking forward to seeing Team Otori.

00:23:39.450 --> 00:23:43.250
You're not going to go
see Tsukigami? To see Kaito?

00:23:44.910 --> 00:23:47.410
Please take care of my brother.

00:23:55.620 --> 00:24:20.250
♪Act 5♪

00:23:56.500 --> 00:23:58.410
Tsukigami, let me borrow your eraser.

00:23:58.410 --> 00:24:00.330
Sure, but what happened to yours?

00:24:00.330 --> 00:24:03.330
I lent it to Toraishi,
but he never gave it back.

00:24:03.330 --> 00:24:06.000
Oh, can I borrow your cellphone charger, too?

00:24:06.000 --> 00:24:08.250
And your shampoo, toothpaste, and pillow...

00:24:08.250 --> 00:24:09.830
Aren't you spoiling him too much?

00:24:10.370 --> 00:24:20.250
♪Otori♪
♪Please be punctual next week, as well.♪
